Introduction","source":{"current_hash_method":"tex-environment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:d4059ccd9a01ca18cf61d21dbc69635420e666ce23bb32a3314887f93d40213c","file":"preprints/Generalized-outer-electron-radii-of-neutral-Coulomb-atoms-September-24-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex","line":38,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"fa04ec940b0f4727966e09e1cb60cf0bb784cc9fea29239208b07e5e3718519c","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Generalized-outer-electron-radii-of-neutral-Coulomb-atoms-September-24-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:d4059ccd9a01ca18cf61d21dbc69635420e666ce23bb32a3314887f93d40213c","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Generalized-outer-electron-radii-of-neutral-Coulomb-atoms-September-24-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex#L38"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{intro:main}\nSet $b_{\\mathrm{TF}}=(81\\pi^2/2)^{1/3}$.  For every choice of normalized\nneutral ground states $(\\Psi_Z)_{Z\\ge1}$ of \\eqref{intro:hamiltonian},\n\\begin{align}\n \\lim_{m\\to\\infty}m^{1/3}\n       \\left[\\limsup_{\\substack{Z\\to\\infty\\\\ Z>m}}R_m(\\Psi_Z)\\right]\n       &=b_{\\mathrm{TF}},\\label{intro:limsup}\\\\\n \\lim_{m\\to\\infty}m^{1/3}\n       \\left[\\liminf_{\\substack{Z\\to\\infty\\\\ Z>m}}R_m(\\Psi_Z)\\right]\n       &=b_{\\mathrm{TF}}.\\label{intro:liminf}\n\\end{align}\nAll limits are over integers.  The inner limits hold $m$ fixed; no\nconvergence in $Z$ at a fixed $m$ is assumed."}
